                <pb facs="0887" n="789" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg789"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102H/326: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-02T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 2, 1919—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your June 9 and 21 regarding Harbin.</p>
                <p>Department giving matter careful consideration but desires consult Consul Moser,
                    expected in Washington soon, before reaching any definite decision.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
